
  ## Application Lifecycle

  1- Not Running
  2- inactive
  3- active
  4- background 
  5- suspended


### 1- Not Running

    App is not in memeory, 

### 2- Inactive

      When you launch an app, or background to foreground, it's inactive for few seconds, fraction of seconds, but the app is in memeory

### 3- Active

      Active is in memeory , in foreground and can take user inputs

### 4- background:

      It's not visible to the user, app is in memeory, code is ruuning and not in foreground

### 5- Suspended

      App will be in mememory but no code will be executed, it will be in background.


## scenePhase

is a SwiftUI environment value that tells you what state your app's UI is currently in — active, inactive, or backgrounded. It's how you detect things like "the user just left the app" or "the user just came back."


## View Modifires

    It shows the appearance of the view

    .font(.title)
    .fontWeight(.bold)


      So these are called View Modifiers 

      .font
      .foregrounfColor
      .fontWeight


    So, this .font . Foreground, .fontWeight is called Chaining


## View Builders

  @ViewBuilder
  it's the mechanism that lets you just list multiple views inside a closure (like inside VStack { } or body) without manually wrapping them in arrays, commas, or return statements.

  
